-- R09 — Crowd asymmetry at the gate: a card on the crowded side is paid less when right and loses more when wrong.
-- Owner request, 24 Oct 2026 (project thread "Add crowding asymmetry to trade EV"), from Ying Hua (ex-Balyasny) on
-- pod-shop investing as poker, not blackjack: when everyone is on the same side, right 60-70% of the time but paid
-- less (everyone sells to monetise), wrong maybe 20% but hit hard (everyone exits together). The card's crowd field
-- (with / against / none) already exists but changed nothing at the gate.
-- Proposed 24 Oct 2026 from a cloud thread with this exact statement (dash.propose_rule raises no approval prompt);
-- apply_after = the next Sunday 20:00 SGT window (Sun 25 Oct 2026), when the Sunday "apply rules" task puts it in
-- force unless the owner replies "oppose R09" to the weekly review email or says no in the thread; both digests then
-- read it through dash.rules_in_force() from the Mon 26 Oct 07:15 SGT run (the same run that starts spec v15's
-- touch targets and hourly-close stops, which is what makes the x1.5 loss leg consistent with realised scoring).
-- Rerunning this file would propose a new rule id, so run it only to re-propose after a revert.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R09' and status = 'proposed';
-- To withdraw it before it applies: select dash.decide_rules('{"withdraw":["R09"]}'::jsonb);
-- Defaults: payoff x0.75 and loss x1.5 when crowd = with; nothing changes for against or none. Calibrated later from
-- the new SCORECARD "crowd:" line (see revert_if). Evidence sources are the ones the digests already read:
-- dash.positioning_extremes() (R02), B7 SATURATION / CAPITULATION, the weekly Grok crowding check, one web statistic.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Crowd asymmetry at the gate: a card on the crowded side is paid less when right and loses more when wrong", "body": "CROWD ASYMMETRY AT THE GATE (owner, 24 Oct 2026). Poker, not blackjack: over a 2-week to 2-month hold the payoff of a trade depends on who else is in it. When a card sits on the crowd's side, being right pays less (the crowd sells into the same catalyst to monetise, so the move stalls short of the thesis target and the exit is worse) and being wrong costs more (the crowd leaves through the same stop, so the hourly-close exit lands beyond it). The crowd's direction is still right more often than not, so this rule never fades a crowd: it changes the payoffs a crowded card is tested on, never its direction. Applies in both books to every candidate at THE TRADE TEST (thematic, tactical, hedge, re-entry; R01 convexity cards as item 5 says), after R08's conflict check and before test (c).\n\n1. CROWD SIDE. Set the card's crowd field from evidence the run has already read, in this order, and print the evidence beside it. WITH = the candidate's direction is the side the crowd is at an extreme on: (i) HARD POSITIONING: dash.positioning_extremes() (R02) lists a directional series (kind spec, retail, flow, sentiment, skew or leverage; never basis or vol) for the candidate's market, or the same underlying in another wrapper, whose read says \"most long\", \"most short\", \"biggest inflow\", \"biggest outflow\", \"most bullish\", \"most bearish\" or \"record\", and the candidate is on that side (a long is WITH \"most long\" or \"biggest inflow\", a short is WITH \"most short\" or \"biggest outflow\"); a \"least long\" or \"least short\" read is the crowd trimming, not an extreme, and never makes a card WITH. (ii) With no table item for that market: a B7 SATURATION or CAPITULATION on the view behind the candidate, the Grok crowding check's crowded verdict for that market dated within 7 days, or one web-found positioning statistic at or beyond the 90th/10th percentile or a record for a series the table does not cover (R02 item 4), each cited with source and date. AGAINST = the candidate's direction is opposite to such a crowd. NONE = neither, or the evidence is price only. SPENT: when the proxy has already moved 2 ATR(20) or more against the crowd since the reading's as-of date (the table's \"since\" move, or the MARK SCRIPT's bars), the extreme is spent: crowd = none, printed \"crowd extreme spent (moved <x> since <date>)\". The card and the TESTED line print \"crowd <with / against / none> - <evidence, 12 words or fewer, source, as-of date>\"; META crowd keeps the one word.\n\n2. ARITHMETIC, test (c), crowd = WITH only: EV = p x r/r x 0.75 - (1 - p) x 1.5, i.e. the payoff when right is cut by a quarter and the loss when wrong is one and a half times 1R. p stays the thesis probability, that the target prints before the stop on the merits, and is not lowered a second time for the crowd (\"the crowd\" is struck from the p reasons on a WITH card; the asymmetry lives in the payoffs). p0 = 1 / (1 + r/r) is unchanged; the crowded break-even is p = 2 / (r/r + 2): 50% at r/r 2.0 (33% unadjusted), 57% at 1.5 (40%), 40% at 3.0 (25%), 67% at 1.0 (50%). Gate unchanged: EV > 0 cards, 0 to +0.30R is THIN EDGE, and \"p at gate\" (pgate) is the lowest 5% step clearing the ADJUSTED EV. crowd = AGAINST and NONE: EV = p x r/r - (1 - p) exactly as the spec has it; the asymmetry that runs in an AGAINST card's favour is never credited, so the record shows whether it exists. Worked example: r/r 2.0, p 45%: unadjusted EV +0.35R; WITH the crowd 0.45 x 1.5 - 0.55 x 1.5 = -0.15R, TESTED and not carded. Under R07 the adjustment applies to the forward r/r.\n\n3. PRINT. A WITH card's EV reads \"EV <+/-x.xxR> (crowd-adjusted; <+/-y.yyR> unadjusted)\" on the full card and the one-line card, and \"EV <+/-x.xxR> (crowd; <+/-y.yyR> raw)\" on the TESTED line; META ev = the adjusted figure, so the dashboard's gate audit, EV buckets and thin-edge tag read the gate value. A WITH lean that fails only because of the adjustment is logged \"not carded (c): crowd asymmetry, EV <+y.yy> -> <-x.xx>\" and its market goes on that day's WASHOUT WATCH line in the opposite direction with \"crowding: <the same evidence>\", the pain trade, where the spec's screen (price extension plus a boundary inside 5 sessions) decides whether it becomes a tactical candidate; nothing is carded on crowding alone. The SCORECARD gains \"crowd: with n/<+/-x.xR> · says <nn%> · hits <nn%> · against n/<+/-x.xR> · says <nn%> · hits <nn%>\" (closed cards by crowd field), so the haircuts can be calibrated.\n\n4. STRUCTURE. On a WITH card the STRUCTURE line names, in 15 words or fewer, the bought-option expression that caps the loss leg (an R01 spread or digital, premium = 1R) and whether the card is carded as one; a linear WITH card keeps its thesis stop.\n\n5. R01 CONVEXITY CARDS. The premium already caps the loss at 1R, so only the payoff side applies: on a WITH card EV = p x rr x 0.75 - (1 - p), with p, p0 and rr as R01 computes them; the gate and THIN EDGE as in R01.\n\n6. FIRST RUN, both books: restate the crowd field with its evidence on every open and pending card (CHANGES line \"Pnn crowd <old> -> <new> (R09): <evidence>\"); no card is closed or re-gated on that alone, EV is an entry gate, but a WITH card whose restated EV is 0 or below carries \"crowd kills the edge\" on its REVIEWS line and the next REVIEW weighs it, as R07 did with carry.", "rationale": "Owner, 24 Oct 2026, from Ying Hua (ex-Balyasny) on pod-shop investing as poker, not blackjack: at a horizon of weeks to months, with similar processes and similar data, everyone is on the same side of the boat; right as a group maybe 60-70% of the time but paid less than expected because everyone sells to monetise, and when wrong, maybe 20% of the time, hit hard because everyone is getting out. The book's crowd field already sits on every card (with / against / none) but changes nothing: the gate tests a crowded card and an uncrowded one on the same payoffs.", "evidence": "dash.trades to 24 Oct 2026: cards tagged crowd = with: Fable 4, Opus 4 (2 closed, both losers: -2.20R view-changed, -1.03R stop); crowd = against: Fable 21, Opus 9. Too few WITH cards to read, which is why the rule is calibrated from the new SCORECARD line rather than set from the record. Voices crowd (dash.crowd_daily since 15 Sep 2026): on one-sided days the market moved the crowd's way over the next 10 sessions 53-58% of the time (26-34 scored days per scope), mean +0.1 to +0.3 sigma: the crowd is right more often than wrong, so the rule adjusts payoffs, never direction. Positioning table, 24 Oct 2026: 14 items at a 3-year extreme or record (EUR speculators most short, Nasdaq leveraged funds most long, TAIEX foreign outflow a record, Henry Hub managed money most short), so WITH is a live condition on several markets most weeks. Defaults (payoff x0.75, loss x1.5) are a judgement: they put the crowded break-even about 15 points above p0, milder than the clip's own numbers (paid two-thirds, lose double), which make a 65%-right crowded trade roughly zero EV.", "revert_if": "Halve the haircuts (x0.875 and x1.25) if, once 20 WITH cards have closed across both books, their realised R averages 0.5R or more above their adjusted-gate EV (too harsh), or if the leans rejected only by the adjustment show a forward outcome of +0.3R or better on average at their review date in the gate audit (the rule is costing good trades); revert if a weekly review finds the crowd side read wrongly (table side misread, \"least long\" treated as an extreme, a spent extreme used) on 2 or more cards within 4 weeks.", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2026-12-05", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
